{
  "$comment": [
    "Source of truth mapping every sheet's grid cells to named animation frames.",
    "scripts/cut-sheets.mjs reads only this file; it never hardcodes a sheet.",
    "",
    "page        which atlas page this sheet's frames are packed into, 1 by",
    "            default. Each page is packed, quantised and written on its own",
    "            and carries its own 400 KB budget, so a roster too big for one",
    "            page spreads over several. A page has its own 256-colour",
    "            palette, so moving a sheet between pages shifts the exact",
    "            pixel colours of every sheet sharing either page; nothing may",
    "            assert an atlas colour it did not read from the texture.",
    "",
    "cols/rows   the grid the sheet was authored on. The cutter divides the image",
    "            by cols x rows and never looks for the drawn grid lines, because",
    "            the art agent returned every sheet at a slightly different pixel",
    "            size than the prompt asked for (hero is 1264x848, not 1152x768).",
    "sheetCell   the authored cell size in px. nativeCell is sheetCell / 4, and",
    "            that is the size each cut frame is downscaled to.",
    "rowSpecs    one entry per grid row, top to bottom. Each row lists the",
    "            animation segments it holds; `cols` is an inclusive 1-based",
    "            column range. Columns not covered by any segment are declared",
    "            blank and the cutter fails if it finds art there. When the same",
    "            anim+facing appears on a later row its frames continue numbering",
    "            (the boss death runs across two rows).",
    "allowEdge   sides on which this row's art is deliberately cut off by the",
    "            sheet border, relaxing the 'bbox touches the cell edge' check on",
    "            those sides only. Two rows need it and both are intentional: the",
    "            fast enemy's spawn flame and the bolt falling in from off-screen.",
    "centred     true for art drawn radiating from the cell centre. The crop box",
    "            is mirrored about that centre and held one native px off the",
    "            art, so the effect comes out whole and centred on its anchor",
    "            rather than flush against a box it exactly fills. Off by",
    "            default: the box is left where the art sits, which is what",
    "            keeps a feet-anchored walk cycle steady, and frames the game",
    "            measures (the boulder, the chain strip) read their own size.",
    "",
    "alphaThreshold  a sheet delivered with an alpha channel only. Alpha at or",
    "            above this is made fully opaque and everything below it is",
    "            cleared, colour and all, before the cell is measured or cut.",
    "            Off (0) by default, because a sheet whose soft edges are the",
    "            art -- the meteor, the fire column's impact -- must keep them.",
    "            The CO-124 companions need it: they arrive as a soft matte with",
    "            no fully opaque pixel anywhere, so at native alpha one figure's",
    "            glow reaches into the next cell and the bounds of both are",
    "            wrong. 240 is the settled value there. Raise it until the cut",
    "            passes rather than reaching for allowEdge, which only silences",
    "            the check and leaves the neighbour's halo in the frame.",
    "",
    "opaque      true for a sheet whose art fills every cell edge to edge: the",
    "            arena's ground and edge tiles (#120). Each cell is taken whole",
    "            and fully opaque, with no colour key (the tile's own colour sits",
    "            at the cell corner) and no edge-overrun check (the art runs off",
    "            every edge on purpose). Keep sheetCell a multiple of 4 so the",
    "            downscale lands on whole source pixels and the tile stays",
    "            seamless."
  ],
